  "term": "genetic programming",
  "definition": "Genetic programming is an evolutionary machine-learning method used to build predictive models from complex, nonlinear data. In this packet, a multi-gene form of genetic programming was used to develop a prognostic model and generate robust predictions from experimental measurements.",
